245
00:40:08,601 --> 00:40:14,221
隣り合った絵の具一つ一つの相乗効果を計算し、絵の具の塊から温度感や湿度感を感じることができる風景へと変貌する表現は、モネが生涯かけて研究していたものです。
Calculating the synergistic effect of each adjacent paint color and transforming it into a scenery where you can feel the warmth and humidity from the lumps of paint is something Monet spent his whole life researching.

246
00:40:14,541 --> 00:40:20,021
光を求めたモネが印象のない日本の浮世絵に強く惹かれたのも理解できますね。
It's understandable that Monet, who sought light, was strongly drawn to Japanese ukiyo-e, which lacked shadows.

247
00:40:20,241 --> 00:40:27,541
彼の絵画の明るさは画家としての研究の成果であり、情熱さえ感じられるそんな作品だと私は感じます。
I feel that the brightness of his paintings is the result of his research as a painter, and a work where you can even feel his passion.

