Many of you probably have the image of "Sunflowers" when you think of Van Gogh. And for good reason—actually, Van Gogh didn't just paint one "Sunflowers".

339
00:57:38,375 --> 00:57:43,425
この世界に失われたものも含めて、7つの「ひまわり」があったんですよ。
Including the ones lost to this world, there were seven "Sunflowers".

340
00:57:43,575 --> 00:57:51,975
さて、では実際に作品をじっくり見てみましょう。みんなはどんな感想を持ったかな？
Now, let's actually take a close look at the artwork. What impressions did everyone have?

341
00:57:52,075 --> 00:58:01,025
改めて見ると、いろんなことが見えてきます。よく見ると、ひまわりの向きはバラバラで、花びらも不揃いですね。
Looking at it again, various things become apparent. If you look closely, the directions of the sunflowers are all scattered, and the petals are uneven.

342
00:58:01,125 --> 00:58:08,075
しかし、温かな黄色が画面全体を包み込むことで、どこか生命力が溢れているようにも見えませんか？
However, doesn't the warm yellow enveloping the whole screen somehow make it look full of vitality?

343
00:58:08,375 --> 00:58:14,975
ここからはゴッホと黄色、そしてゴッホと「ひまわり」について紐解いていきましょう。
From here, let's unravel the connection between Van Gogh and yellow, and Van Gogh and "Sunflowers".

344
00:58:15,375 --> 00:58:25,075
太陽は淡い異用の輝きを伝達するのだ、という言葉を残しているゴッホは、太陽の光を黄色で表現しました。
Leaving behind the words "The sun transmits a pale, strange radiance," Van Gogh expressed the light of the sun in yellow.

345
00:58:25,275 --> 00:58:30,175
そして黄色はゴッホにとって生命力の象徴でもあります。
And yellow is also a symbol of vitality for Van Gogh.

346
00:58:30,375 --> 00:58:43,775
この絵を描いた時、彼はフランス南部のアールルという街で新天地、画家として仲間と頑張っていこうと意気込んでいました。そんな気持ちを黄色に託したのかも知れません。
When he painted this picture, he was enthusiastic about working hard with friends as a painter in a new place called Arles in southern France. Perhaps he entrusted such feelings to yellow.

347
00:58:44,075 --> 00:58:49,375
一方で、この絵のモチーフになっている「ひまわり」について見てみましょう。
On the other hand, let's look at "Sunflowers," which is the motif of this painting.

348
00:58:49,475 --> 00:58:56,625
ひまわりは太陽に向かって咲きます。太陽は西洋美術史において神を象徴します。
Sunflowers bloom facing the sun. The sun symbolizes God in Western art history.

349
00:58:56,875 --> 00:59:07,475
それに向かって咲くひまわりは、崇拝、従順、忠実、そして信仰心や愛を象徴します。
Sunflowers blooming toward it symbolize worship, obedience, loyalty, and faith or love.

350
00:59:07,675 --> 00:59:13,125
ここでさらに遠回りして、彼の過去について知っていきましょう。
Let's take a further detour here and learn about his past.

351
00:59:13,275 --> 00:59:20,525
先ほどゴッホがアールルでの生活を始めた時、私は「新天地！」という表現をしました。
Earlier, when Van Gogh started his life in Arles, I used the expression "A new realm!"

352
00:59:20,675 --> 00:59:25,475
実は彼、元々は牧師さんになりたかったんです。
Actually, he originally wanted to become a pastor.

353
00:59:25,725 --> 00:59:31,375
彼は頑張って勉強や布教活動に注力しますが、うまくいきませんでした。
He tried hard and focused on studying and missionary work, but it didn't go well.

354
00:59:31,625 --> 00:59:36,875
画家への転身は牧師さんへの道を断たれた後のことだったんですね。
Turning to painting was something that happened after the path to becoming a pastor was cut off.

355
00:59:37,075 --> 00:59:45,175
そんな彼が描く信仰の象徴である「ひまわり」、皆様はどう読み解きますか？
How do you interpret "Sunflowers," which is a symbol of faith painted by such a man?

356
00:59:45,375 --> 00:59:54,575
未来への希望の光？それとも自分への失望？ゴッホの見出した光のすみかは「ひまわり」にあったのかもしれませんね。
The light of hope for the future? Or disappointment in himself? The dwelling place of light that Van Gogh found might have been in "Sunflowers."

357
00:59:54,775 --> 01:00:01,630
という感じでございまして、こちらもロンドンのナショナル・ギャラリーさんにて見ることができます！
With that said, you can also see this at The National Gallery in London!

358
01:01:59,867 --> 01:02:06,907
暗がりステージに立つ 雨傘を携え
Standing on the darkened stage, holding an umbrella in hand,

359
01:02:07,607 --> 01:02:13,547
朧に霞む構図 印象 儚く
A faintly hazy composition, fleeting and impressionistic.

360
01:02:15,227 --> 01:02:18,347
始めましょ 雨粒ドローイング
Let's begin our raindrop drawing,

361
01:02:18,787 --> 01:02:23,727
キャンバスはこの空、この世界
The canvas is this sky, this world!

362
01:02:25,387 --> 01:02:30,647
Hop Hop 飛び回る Tap Tap 打ち鳴らす Dance Dance ぐるぐる いざ…！
Hop, hop, darting around! Tap, tap, striking the beat! Dance, dance, spinning in circles, now...!

363
01:02:32,047 --> 01:02:35,427
Ladies and Gentlemen, Welcome to our magical show!

364
01:02:36,427 --> 01:02:39,107
スポットライトを浴びて
Bathed in the spotlight,

365
01:02:39,427 --> 01:02:42,487
輝きを放つ
Emanating a brilliant glow,

366
01:02:43,727 --> 01:02:48,367
エンタシスよりプリズム 分光をスタンバイ
A prism surpassing entasis, standby for dispersion!

367
01:02:48,967 --> 01:02:52,187
この鈍色の空に七色の橋を架けて見せましょう
Let's bridge this dull grey sky with a rainbow of seven colors

368
01:02:52,687 --> 01:02:57,307
さあさ、とくとご覧あれ！
Now, behold with your own eyes!

369
01:02:57,607 --> 01:03:02,287
目に映るもの、今を彩るから
For whatever reflects in our eyes colors the present moment,

370
01:03:02,507 --> 01:03:06,807
大きな絵筆で描き出す 大胆なパースの中
Painting with a giant paintbrush amidst a daring perspective,

371
01:03:09,947 --> 01:03:15,867
びしょ濡れの舞台は ミラクルなパレット
This soaked stage is a miraculous palette!

372
01:03:21,807 --> 01:03:26,127
マスカレードな第二部の開演
The masquerade's second act curtain rises,

373
01:03:27,507 --> 01:03:31,327
Shall we dance? モノトーンから極彩色に
Shall we dance? From monochrome to vivid colors,

374
01:03:32,707 --> 01:03:36,607
アシンメトリーなグラデーションで
With an asymmetrical gradation,

375
01:03:36,667 --> 01:03:39,527
夢中になってほしいの
I want you to be completely captivated,

376
01:03:39,707 --> 01:03:43,327
雨雲にマーブリング
Marbling the rain clouds.

377
01:03:43,507 --> 01:03:48,907
目を奪われたその隙に イリュージョンをスタンバイ
In the brief moment your eyes were stolen, standby for illusion!

378
01:03:49,967 --> 01:03:53,967
ところで皆さん、なくし物はございませんか？
By the way everyone, is anyone missing something?

379
01:03:55,327 --> 01:03:57,807
どなた様もおいでませ！
Welcome, one and all!

380
01:03:58,527 --> 01:04:02,227
あの手この手で魅了していくから
I'll captivate you by every means possible,

381
01:04:03,007 --> 01:04:07,287
一足お先に まんまと盗みだすわ
Stealing it away cleanly just a step ahead,

382
01:04:07,627 --> 01:04:11,287
あなたの心を 光を放ち出す
Your heart, letting loose a light,

383
01:04:11,587 --> 01:04:16,307
きらめきのパレット
A sparkling palette!

384
01:04:17,167 --> 01:04:21,887
さてさて、いよいよ大詰め クライマックスに向けて盛り上がってまいりましょう！ Listen!
Now then, finally heading toward the climax, let's get even more hyped! Listen!

385
01:04:25,647 --> 01:04:31,467
OK, 5・4・3・2・1 Go on the Show!
OK, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, Go on the Show!

386
01:04:36,667 --> 01:04:41,587
最大級のキャンバスに描き出す
Painting on the largest scale canvas,

387
01:04:43,407 --> 01:04:48,967
誰も見たことのない景色
A scenery nobody has ever seen before,

388
01:04:51,707 --> 01:04:54,767
さあさ、とくとご覧あれ！
Now, behold with your own eyes!

389
01:04:55,107 --> 01:04:59,287
次元の壁を超えて閃くから
Flashing across dimensional boundaries,

390
01:04:59,547 --> 01:05:03,511
大きな絵筆で描き出す
Painting with a giant paintbrush...

391
01:05:03,631 --> 01:05:06,711
大胆なバスの中さ
In a daring bus...

392
01:05:07,611 --> 01:05:12,411
みんなで大円団へ迎えに行こう
Let's all go welcome the grand finale!

393
01:05:13,911 --> 01:05:19,711
びしょ濡れの舞台はミラクルなパレット
This drenched stage is a miraculous palette!

